# Optional inference boundary

Keep heavy inference dependencies out of the default application and pack reader. This does not require a dedicated microservice for each transformation.

- Source collection, deterministic extraction, hashing, lexical indexing and reading should work without model calls. Use ordinary library functions for lightweight deterministic work.
- Do not add torch, transformers, sentence-transformers or equivalent transitive model-loading dependencies to the default reader/API image.
- If embeddings, reranking, classification or generated summaries demonstrate a needed benefit, invoke an explicitly configured existing endpoint or run an isolated, bounded batch job. Do not provision a permanent service fleet by default.
- Keep model/revision, dimensions and extraction settings with derived data. Preserve original sources and permit rebuilding the index without generated enrichment.
- Report build and refresh cost alongside query cost. Missing optional enrichment must not prevent access to valid source evidence.
- Do not assume cluster DNS endpoints, a keyword service, TEI, a BGE service or any running model exists. Existing service clients are reuse candidates, not deployment requirements.

Follow the [architecture decision record](docs/ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md) for scope. Keep untrusted extraction/execution isolated from long-lived credentials even when reducing process count.
